      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "To synchronize the bloodstream along the shunt and the bloodflow along coronary channel hemodynamically protected aortocoronary shunt was elaborated and applied in 1 patient. The monocusp was formed, dipped in the aorta lumen by means of V-figurative cut in the ascending aorta wall. An aperture in the aorta wall, disposed behind the monocusp in direction of bloodstream, was closed with the autovena patch, in centre of which the section was made and the autovenous transplant was sewn along its edge."},
